      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Chinese Ten",
          "subtitle": "Card game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Chinese Ten (Jiǎn Hóng Diǎn / 拣红点): Chinese fishing game. Play a card to capture a layout card (pairs sum to 10, or same rank for 10/J/Q/K); then flip one from deck. Related to Thai Red Frog Black Frog and Indonesian Main Merah."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "China. Jiǎn Hóng Diǎn (pick up red spots). Oriental fishing style: card flipped from deck after each play. Similar to Thai Gob Dum Gob Dang and Indonesian Main Merah."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2, 3, or 4. Each gets 24÷n cards (e.g. 2p=12 each, 4p=6 each)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52 cards. Numeral 1–9 capture by sum to 10; Ten and pictures capture same rank only."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52-card deck; layout space for 4+ cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 24÷n cards each. Four cards turned face up as initial layout. Rest face down."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
